# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values there.
#
#   .env.local is git-ignored. NEVER put a real password in this file
#   (.env.example IS committed) and never commit .env or .env.local.
#
# On Vercel these go in: Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# (Production + Preview). Redeploy after adding or changing them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Contact form (SMTP) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used ONLY on the server, inside src/app/api/contact/route.ts.
# Deliberately NOT prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that prefix would ship the
# value to the browser, which would leak the password to every visitor.
#
# For Gmail: SMTP_USER is the full address, and SMTP_PASSWORD must be a
# 16-character *App Password* (Google Account → Security → 2-Step
# Verification → App passwords), not your normal account password.
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Optional — defaults suit Gmail. Override for another provider.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# Where contact messages are delivered. Defaults to SMTP_USER.
# CONTACT_TO=

# ── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASSWORD are not set, the contact form does not pretend
# to send: the API replies 503 and the UI falls back to opening the visitor's
# own mail client with the message pre-filled. Nothing silently disappears.
